Q: calling operators of base class... safe? A: <p>That's better to use</p>
<pre><code>Base::operator=(rhs);
</code></pre>
<p>because if your base class have a pure virtual method the static_cast is not allowed.</p>
<pre><code>class Base {
    // Attribute
    public:
        virtual void f() = 0;
    protected:
        Base&amp; operator=(const Base&amp;);
}

class Derived : public Base {
    public:
        virtual void f() {};
        Derived&amp; operator=(const Derived&amp; src) {
            Base::operator=(src); // work
            static_cast&lt;Base&amp;&gt;(*this) = src; // didn't work
        }
}
</code></pre>
